  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\n04\nAug\nBYDUNCAN PARSONS// VISIT US, WHATSON\nSOFO Summer Shelter Competition\nSOFO Summer Shelter Competition!\n\nTo celebrate our recently opened Anderson Shelter display (built with the support of our wonderful Crowdfunder backers!) we're running a special competition this Summer - show us your own home-made air-raid shelters and we'll award prizes to the best! Plus, we'll feature submissions in an online gallery - so they'll all be museum pieces!\n\nHere are a couple of examples of shelters crafted by the museum team's families to give you an idea of what we're looking for - can you build better?\n\nWho can join in?\n\nThere will be two categories, and prizes for the best in each:\n\nAges 11+\nUnder 11s\nHow do we enter?\n\nSend us a photo of your creation, or bring it with you on a visit to the museum, and let us know which category you're competing in, plus leave us with a name and contact detail we can use if your shelter is picked!\n\nYou can send us a picture of your shelter via email, send us a direct message on our social media accounts, or post them in the comments below the competition post.\n\nWhat can you win?\n\nWin a family annual pass, covering museum entry for two adults and up to four children for a whole year!\n\nPlus, bring your shelter in with you, or a photo of it, when you visit the museum and get a free child day admission.\n\nWhen does the competition end?\n\nThe closing date for the competion will be 30th September 2022, we'll contact and announce winners shortly after!\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nOne competition entry per child, though households with multiple children wishing to submit a shelter for the competition can submit one entry from each child. These terms also apply to the free child day admission offer open to all competition entrants.\n\nSelected winners will be contacted shortly after the closing date using the contact detail left with us for the purposes of the competition, or if your entry was submitted via social media, we'll attempt to contact winners by direct message on the social media platform the winning entry was submitted on. Your contact details will not be used for marketing or any other purposes, but if you would like updates on events and exhibitions at the museum, please join our mailing list here.\n\n Tags: Anderson Shelter, Blitz, competition, crafts, families, Museum, summer, summer holidays, Whats On, Win\n\nPrevious:\nWinston Churchill, Blenheim Palace, and the Oxfordshire Yeomanry Connection\nNext:\nThe Man Behind the Medals: Major John Windham Meade\nRelated posts\nOBJECT OF THE MONTH: EVACUEE’S COAT (OXFORDSHIRE’S MILITARY HERITAGE IN 50 OBJECTS)\n\nEvacuee’s Coat from our Oxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects Exhibition By Geraldine Howell Object photography by Colin Morris Philip Williams’ woollen, fully-lined children’s coat would certainly have satisfied the requirement for evacuees to take with them a warm winter coat as they moved from their homes to safer locations elsewhere, often in the countryside. This smart, yet also sensible and practical design, very much reflected the type of coat…\n\nOBJECT OF THE MONTH FEBRUARY 2026: SWEETHEART PIN CUSHION\n\nFebruary’s Object of the Month follows a Valentine’s Day theme! Volunteer Geraldine has selected a First World War pin cushion, shaped like a heart, it has quite a story behind it! Sweetheart Pin Cushion By Geraldine Howell Object photography by Colin Morris   This sweetheart pin cushion was made during the First World War by a member of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry. Sweetheart cushions were not unknown before…\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
